"""
=============================================================================
  KAN-MTS Financial Dataset Builder
  -----------------------------------
  Builds a real, long-history multivariate time-series CSV suitable for
  KAN temporal research experiments.

  OUTPUT COLUMNS (matching your sample schema):
    Date, Open_Price, Close_Price, High_Price, Low_Price, Volume,
    Daily_Return_Pct, Volatility_Range, VIX_Close,
    Economic_News_Flag, Sentiment_Score,
    Federal_Rate_Change_Flag, GeoPolitical_Risk_Score, Currency_Index

  SOURCES:
    - Yahoo Finance  (yfinance)         → OHLCV, VIX, DXY
    - FRED API       (fredapi)          → Fed Funds Rate
    - Dallas Fed GPR (HTTP download)    → Geopolitical Risk Score
    - Baker-Bloom EPU(HTTP download)    → Economic Policy Uncertainty
                                          (used as proxy for News Flag + Sentiment)

  HISTORY:  1990-01-01  →  today   (longest period with all features available)
            VIX starts 1990; GPR starts 1985; FRED goes back to 1954.

  INSTALL (run once):
    pip install --upgrade yfinance fredapi pandas numpy requests tqdm openpyxl

  FRED API KEY:
    Free from https://fred.stlouisfed.org/docs/api/api_key.html
    Set it below or via environment variable FRED_API_KEY.

  USAGE:
    python data_prep.py

  KAN-MTS COMPATIBILITY:
    The script also saves a PyTorch-ready .pt file with the tensors:
      x_enc      (N, seq_len, enc_in)   ← input window
      x_mark_enc (N, seq_len, 4)        ← time features [month,day,weekday,hour]
      x_dec      (N, label+pred, enc_in)
      x_mark_dec (N, label+pred, 4)
      y          (N, pred_len, enc_in)  ← ground truth

    Default: seq_len=96, pred_len=96, label_len=48 (change below).
=============================================================================
"""

